  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-264857/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-j-j-ballet6-e-gouba7-m-gentilini8.md",
      "source_hash": "bf231689f159f4f4911cd9137bb911a179b598b90fd8b7856a6ed45f81664c4d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Opens a 1982 French-language study of tetanus vaccination in rural African children, reporting that after one or two doses of adsorbed toxoid nearly all children reached protective antibody levels, with higher levels after two doses. It notes that moderate malnutrition and Plasmodium falciparum infection had no detectable short-term effect on antibody response, while unweaned children responded better after a single dose. The introduction explains why a shorter vaccination schedule matters where health infrastructure is weak, and the methods begin describing the children studied and the vaccine and dosing used.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-264857/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-programme.md",
      "source_hash": "02f1906c82dd038f996372b854d16563b74f80c8ce3e5ab3820b77335d73655c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes how children were classed as well nourished or malnourished by weight against reference norms and how malaria infection was assessed by blood smear, with intermediate-weight children excluded. It also outlines a preliminary check for pre-existing tetanus immunity in two groups of young children from an isolated village and a town with a dispensary.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-264857/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-un.md",
      "source_hash": "c476b11823b0edfa8387ae461ed9cb1f8c66f61c20978002344760b2878f87ba",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Details the blood sampling schedule, cold-chain transport of samples to a laboratory in Ouagadougou, and the separation of plasma for antibody testing. It then presents results on antibody levels after one or two injections, comparing groups by nutritional status, weaning and malaria infection. Figures show the distribution of antitetanus antibody titres among malaria-infected and uninfected children.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
