    {
      "block": "library/10665-264857/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-bonne.md",
      "source_hash": "fe02ded802155076d292b10e649e1c8385eb1d13508cdef5e9616e5f6772c4d7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses the reliability of the radioimmunoassay used and the limited survey of pre-vaccination immunity, which suggested more natural exposure in the isolated rural village but on too small a sample to conclude. It considers why malnutrition and malaria did not appear to impair the antibody response and the effect of breastfeeding. The authors conclude cautiously that malaria had no significant effect on antitetanus antibody responses in children aged 1 to 3 years and that any effect of antimalarial drugs cannot be determined.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
