      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The English summary of the antibody findings, reporting that nearly all of 414 children aged 1-3 years reached measurable antitetanus antibody levels after one or two toxoid doses, with two doses giving higher levels. It adds that nutritional status and malaria infection made no difference, while breastfed children responded better after one dose only.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
